## DEFINITION
PROCHECK is a protein structure validation tool that assesses the stereochemical quality of a 3D protein model.

## PURPOSE
- Validate protein structures.
- Assess stereochemical quality.
- Detect structural errors.
- Improve model reliability.

## MAIN ANALYSIS
- Ramachandran plot analysis.
- Bond length and bond angle evaluation.
- Dihedral angle assessment.
- Residue geometry validation.

## IMPORTANT RESULT
- Ramachandran plot showing favored, allowed, and disallowed regions.
- Percentage of residues in favored regions.
- Overall stereochemical quality of the protein model.

## FILES TO UPLOAD
- PDB (.pdb) protein structure file.

## IMPORTANT POINTS
- Widely used for protein structure validation.
- Evaluates stereochemical accuracy of protein models.
- Commonly used with ERRAT and Verify3D.
- Higher percentage of residues in favored regions indicates a better-quality model.
